Syrin is a [[Phenomena/Locality|locality]] near the core of the [[Geography/index|Astra]]. The whole of the planet is held in what its people call the Rhett, a dream laid over the world, and the life of Syrin runs through it as a single weave.

Its people are far ahead of [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]]: they have had trains and firearms for a long time, and most carry machinery worked into the body, which they call chrome, some of it set in the womb. The chrome is the way into the Rhett. A flat, paper-thin implant set at the base of the skull and a port cut into the neck let a person see the Rhett laid over the world, thread themselves to every electronic thing around them, hold credit, and carry an identity. It is also how they are reached: [[Org/Omnivox/index|Omnivox]] holds much of that access, and those it takes over move under its hand.

They keep no coin and no guard. A stranger with gold in hand has nothing to trade, because credit is held and spent through the Rhett, by means an outsider cannot work.

The great city of [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Terminus|Terminus]] stands on Syrin.
